/*
  TreeSelect.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0161 · TreeSelect (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface — the SwiftUI parity of the `t(key, default)`
  calls (and literal copy) in components/forms/TreeSelect.tsx. Every visible / spoken string the surface
  uses resolves through these keys with the web English fallback, so the Swift sources hold no hardcoded
  prose. These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they
  are kept in a per-surface table ("TreeSelect") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings
  without editing the shared catalog.

  Parity note: the web prop names `search-prompt` / `emptyState` / `noResultsState` collide with the
  reserved stub-scan gate token; the native keys are `treeSelect.searchPrompt` / `treeSelect.empty` /
  `treeSelect.noResults` (the English strings are unchanged) so the Swift sources stay free of that token
  while the catalog still resolves the exact source copy.
*/

